   "classification": "HARNESS",
   "classification_evidence": "ubuntu 3.14 only (4576 ran, errors=1; the same commit passed on ubuntu 3.11/3.12/3.13, and locally 4579 OK): the V1 test helper tests/test_closure.py::Repo.close raised OSError [Errno 39] Directory not empty: '/tmp/tmpms1248ti/.git' from TemporaryDirectory.cleanup. Measured cause (GIT_TRACE=1 on a fresh repository, git 2.53/2.55): `git commit` spawns `git maintenance run --auto --quiet --detach`, a detached child that writes into .git while the helper is already removing the repository — a race of the V1 test harness, HARNESS: not PRODUCT (aisef/ untouched, V1 evidence byte-identical), not DEVELOPER (no V2 test, no V2 code in the traceback), not ENVIRONMENT (the runner did what git asked). No V1-PF-001 signature; owned processes 0/0/0, escaped 0, released_empty True. Not rerun: the fix candidate (the helper runs git with maintenance.auto=false and gc.auto=0) is validated by its own first run.",
