   "classification": "PRODUCT",
   "classification_evidence": "windows 3.11 only (4573 ran, errors=1; the same commit passed on ubuntu 3.11/3.12/3.13 and locally): test_memory.IntegrationTests.test_concurrent_writers, a V1 test of the frozen tree, errored with PermissionError [Errno 13] Permission denied from os.write(fd, b'\\0') in aisef/_compat.py::flock_ex_nb (called by aisef/memory.py::_locked): the Windows shim writes the lock file's first byte itself when the file is empty, so two first writers racing on a brand-new store can have one write into the byte the other just locked; the shim translates only msvcrt.locking's error to BlockingIOError, never os.write's, and _locked retries BlockingIOError only. PRODUCT: a latent defect of the frozen V1 tree (aisef/ is not modified; the same test failed once before this program, D-020 notes), Windows-only, first occurrence in the V2 program's CI logs; not DEVELOPER (no V2 code, no V2 test), not HARNESS (the test's writers did what the product asks), not ENVIRONMENT. No V1-PF-001 signature; owned processes 0/0/0, escaped 0, released_empty True. Not rerun: the fix candidate seeds the lock byte in the V1 test so CI measures the twenty writers the test is about; the defect is reported for the owner's V1 backlog, not fixed.",
